\sgaStableTarget{sga6.e00.prop.1-5}\textbf{Proposition 1.5.} \emph{Let $A$ be a commutative graded ring with unit, $N$ an element of $\widetilde A$ of the form $N=[q,1+N^1+\cdots+N^q]$, and $x$ an arbitrary element of $\widetilde A$: $x=[\nu,1+\sum_{i\geq1}x^i]$. Then, for every integer $j\geq1$, we have $\gamma^{q+j}(N,x)\in\widetilde A^j$, and the component of degree $j$ of $\gamma^{q+j}(N,x)$ is of the form}
